{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1784881825,"nonce":"XtCsPG/bQAyUMKMVIqTbLjEdePI=","target":"998f20bb369df2326efa218505193514c801e6394f8c5a3bac006b16805c556d","message":"**Parent:** ADR-0060 — Org settings surface (`docs/adr/0060-org-settings-connections-and-secret-management.md`).\n\n**What to build**\n\nIntroduce the `/v1/connections` **read** API and a **Connections** section in global Settings, with GitHub as an **observe-only** surface. Installing the GitHub App *is* registration (the installation webhook already auto-creates the connection and binds repos), so there is no create path for GitHub — the UI reflects state and offers healing, not creation.\n\nThe section lists each `ForgeConnection` with its bound Projects (derived from `forge_repos`), the forge kind + base URL, and credential/delivery health (does `credential_ref` resolve? recent webhook deliveries?). For a GitHub connection it offers a **\"Manage on GitHub →\"** deep link to the installation settings and a **re-sync** action that re-fetches `installation_repositories` to heal a missed webhook.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- [ ] `GET /v1/connections` returns connections + their bound Projects + health, `Administer`-gated; OpenAPI + UI client regenerated.\n- [ ] Connections section renders the list with kind, base URL, bound Projects, and credential/delivery health.\n- [ ] GitHub connection shows a working \"Manage on GitHub →\" deep link.\n- [ ] A re-sync action re-fetches installation repositories and reconciles `forge_repos` (a repo added on GitHub while a webhook was missed appears after re-sync).\n- [ ] Credentials are never returned by the API (health is a boolean/status, not the secret).\n- [ ] Functional test: list endpoint with a fake connection store, Administer enforcement, and re-sync reconciliation.\n\n**Blocked by:** d2cee7d (Slice 1: Global Settings shell) — needs the `/settings` route + Administer gate.","files":null}]}